    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="11900459-6c18-5b4f-b552-164a9625285a" activityNameId="3e8f4bd1-35d6-5dda-991d-52eecd6db8dd" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Alkyd resin, long oil, 70% in white spirit, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Alkyd resin, long oil, 70% in white spirit, at plant
Alkyds are a large and diverse family of polyesters. Long oil alkyds are often used in architectural paints. This dataset stands for one specific long oil alkyd and should not be used for other alkyds if its contribution to the overall result is im-portant. The data quality is not sufficient to allow for e.g. a comparative assess-ment of different binders of paints.\nTechnology: The dataset models the commonly used solvent process. It assumes the use of soybean oil as fatty acid, phthalic anhydride as polybasic acid and Pentaeritol as polyol.\nVersion: 2.2\nEnergy values: Undefined\nProduction volume: unknown\nLocal category: Lacke &amp; Farben, Leime\nLocal subcategory: Herstellung\nUVEK 2022 source file:01671.XML\n\n
UUID: 5f0c6b59-3400-381b-86e3-7378b6e81df8
Transport of raw materials and production of resin. Packaging is neglected.
Location: undefined
Technology: The dataset models the commonly used solvent process. It assumes the use of soybean oil as fatty acid, phthalic anhydride as polybasic acid and Pentaeritol as polyol.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: A "typical" alkyd is chosen and its raw material consumption is calculated. Energy data are taken from the one source that is known. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5f0c6b59-3400-381b-86e3-7378b6e81df8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
